<title>UK: BP dips as chairman quits to join government.</title>
<headline>BP dips as chairman quits to join government.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Petroleum Co Plc dipped in early trading on Wednesday after reports that its chairman Sir David Simon is to be appointed to a ministerial position in the new Labour government.</p>
<p>The stock was down 2p at 730-1/2 by 0705 GMT, even as the overall market extended Tuesday's sharp gains.</p>
<p>A report in the Financial Times said Simon would be given a job focusing on trade promotion within the Department of Trade and Industry, adding that the move would be a blow to BP's shareholders.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
